Specification Tennis Scoring

DataType TennisScore
Description Textual tennis scores
Examples: ValidValues
| Value              | IsValid | Notes                               |
| Love-All           | True    |                                     |
| Fifteen-Love       | True    |                                     |
| Thirty-Fifteen     | True    |                                     |
| Forty-Thirty       | True    |                                     |
| Deuce              | True    |                                     |
| Advantage Player 1 | True    |                                     |
| Advantage Player 2 | True    |                                     |
| Win For Player 1   | True    |                                     |
| Win For Player 2   | True    |                                     |
| Fifty-Love         | False   | Fifty is not a tennis score.        |
| Advantage          | False   | Advantage must identify the player. |
| Winner Player 1    | False   | Win For is the correct format.      |
|                    | False   | Tennis score must not be empty.     |

Attributes ScoringCases
| Name          | DataType    |
| Player1Points | Integer     |
| Player2Points | Integer     |
| Result        | TennisScore |

Calculation Equal Scores Below Forty
Description Equal scores below three points are expressed using the score name followed by All.
Examples: ScoringCases
| Player1Points | Player2Points | Result      |
| 0             | 0             | Love-All    |
| 1             | 1             | Fifteen-All |
| 2             | 2             | Thirty-All  |

Calculation Ordinary Scores
Description Scores below deuce are expressed using the score names for each player.
Examples: ScoringCases
| Player1Points | Player2Points | Result         |
| 1             | 0             | Fifteen-Love   |
| 2             | 0             | Thirty-Love    |
| 3             | 0             | Forty-Love     |
| 2             | 1             | Thirty-Fifteen |
| 3             | 1             | Forty-Fifteen  |
| 3             |               |                |